TCP = reliable, connection-oriented, full-duplex, byte-stream protocol.

TCP header = 20–60 bytes; scaling factor 4 for header length.

Sequence number = 32-bit; identifies first data byte.

ACK number = next expected byte.

URG → urgent data; PSH → push buffer; RST → reset; SYN → synchronize; FIN → terminate.

Window size = 16-bit; used for flow control; dynamic.

Options = 0–40 bytes; used for timestamp, window scaling, MSS negotiation, padding.

TCP = 75% SR + 25% Go-Back-N.

Wrap Around Time = 2³² / data rate.

