Q8. What are the steps of DVR?

Step-01: Each router prepares its routing table using local knowledge (only neighbors).

Step-02: Each router exchanges its distance vector with its neighbors and prepares a new table using the Bellman-Ford equation.

Repeat Step-02 for (n − 2) times if there are n routers.

After this, routing tables converge / become stable.

Q9. Why is Step-02 repeated (n − 2) times?

To propagate distance information across the entire network.

With n routers, after (n − 2) exchanges, every router has learned the shortest path to every destination — the tables converge.

