Part A: OSPF (Open Shortest Path First)
Q1. What is OSPF?

Open Shortest Path First — an Interior Gateway Protocol (IGP) used for routing within an Autonomous System (AS).

Based on Link State Routing and uses Dijkstra’s algorithm.

Q2. What are the key features of OSPF?

Link-state protocol — every router has the complete topology.

Uses Dijkstra’s shortest path algorithm.

Supports hierarchical routing using areas.

Uses cost as the metric (usually based on bandwidth).

Supports equal-cost multipath (ECMP) — multiple equal-cost routes can be used.

Fast convergence — triggered updates.

Q3. What is the OSPF metric?

Cost — typically inversely proportional to bandwidth.

Formula: 
Cost
