Q14. What is the Jam Signal?

A 48-bit signal released by transmitting stations as soon as they detect a collision.

It alerts other stations not to transmit immediately after the collision.

Prevents another collision with the same data packet.

Ethernet sends the jam signal at a frequency different from data signals → ensures jam signal does not collide with collided data signals.

Q15. What is Back-off Time?

After collision, the station waits for a random amount of time called back-off time.

After back-off time, it retries transmission.

If collision occurs again → waits another random back-off time and retries.

Continues until the back-off limit is reached → then aborts transmission.

