Q6. What is Slotted Aloha?

Divides the shared channel time into discrete intervals (time slots).

Stations can transmit only at the beginning of a time slot.

If the beginning is missed → wait for the next slot.

Collision occurs if two or more stations transmit at the beginning of the same slot.

